@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "User Data Deletion";
}

<section class="page-section">

    <h1 class="section-title">
        USER DATA DELETION
    </h1>

    <p class="section-subtitle">
        How to request deletion of your PonyUp Performance account data.
    </p>

    <div class="price-card"
         style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;text-align:left;min-height:0;">

        <h2>REQUEST ACCOUNT DELETION</h2>

        <p>
            To request deletion of personal information associated with
            your PonyUp Performance account, send an email from the address
            associated with your PonyUp account.
        </p>

        <p>
            Email:
            <a href="mailto:lopezkb258@gmail.com?subject=PonyUp%20Data%20Deletion%20Request">
                lopezkb258@gmail.com
            </a>
        </p>

        <p>
            Use the subject line
            <strong>PonyUp Data Deletion Request</strong>
            and include the email address associated with the account.
        </p>

        <p>
            Do not send your password, payment-card information, or other
            sensitive credentials by email.
        </p>

        <h2>VERIFICATION</h2>

        <p>
            PonyUp may verify that the requester controls the account before
            deleting account information. This protects users from unauthorized
            deletion requests.
        </p>

        <h2>THIRD-PARTY SERVICES</h2>

        <p>
            Information held independently by payment processors, external
            sign-in providers, or other third-party services is governed by
            those providers' own retention and deletion policies.
        </p>

        <h2>QUESTIONS</h2>

        <p>
            For privacy questions or help with a deletion request, use the
            <a asp-page="/Contact">Contact page</a>.
        </p>

    </div>

</section>
